    "q-106970": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106970",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{33}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,0\\,\\, & \\,-3\\, & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{21}=1$ and ${u}_{33}=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{33}=1\\cdot (-1)=-1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
